.PP
For the computation of the nodal 'gravity force'

.PP
Hardwired variables: 'fluid density' 'dry rock density' 'porosity' 'permeability' 'conductivity' 'gravity term' for hydrostatic fluid pressure gradient 'gravity force' for body forces acting on the rock skeleton 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::OverburdenPressureVisitor\fP< dim >::Visit (\fBElement\fP< dim > * e)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
this method computes all the element properties 'K' and 'gravity term', etc\&. Loops over the element integration points and evaluates shear and tensile failure potential\&. Where failure occurred the variable 'failure' is set to 1\&. A distinction is made between tensile 'failure01' and shear failure 'failure' variables\&.

.PP
